@@ replace
If this skill ran in a session launched inside the new folder, note that the freshly written `CLAUDE.md` and memory dir won't be in context until a fresh window is opened ("Reload Window" doesn't pick them up).
@@ with
Future Codex sessions started in the project discover its `AGENTS.md` automatically. If you continue in this chat, the freshly written `AGENTS.md` is not in context yet — read it explicitly before relying on it.

@@ replace
Never overwrite existing `CLAUDE.md`, `.git`, or other user content.
@@ with
Never overwrite existing `AGENTS.md`, `.git`, or other user content. A project that already has a `CLAUDE.md` (from Claude Code) keeps it — leave it alone and create `AGENTS.md` alongside.

@@ replace
